# Student management & error handling

**Severity:** Medium
**Area:** student routes, error handling middleware, input validation

## Problems

### 1. Error pages return raw JSON

Visiting a non-existent URL (`/nonexistent`), an out-of-bounds activity index, or triggering a 403 all return bare JSON like `{"detail":"Not Found"}` — no HTML, no nav, no way to navigate back. This is the default FastAPI error response and is confusing for students.

**Fix:** Add an exception handler (or middleware) that renders a user-friendly error template for 404 and 403 responses, with navigation and a link back to `/lezione/`.

### 2. No way to delete student accounts

The student list grows with every created account. There's no delete button or account management. Over time the student selection page becomes cluttered.

**Fix:** Add a delete button (with confirmation) on each student card, or on the profile page. `DELETE /students/{id}` currently returns 404, so the route needs to be implemented.

### 3. No input validation on student names

- **No length limit:** A 140+ character name is accepted and breaks the nav layout
- **No character restrictions:** Special characters are accepted (though properly escaped — no XSS)
- **Duplicate names allowed:** Two students named "Marco" can be created with no warning, making them indistinguishable on the selection page

**Fix:**
- Add a max-length constraint (e.g. 30 characters) on the `name` field, both in the HTML `<input maxlength>` and server-side
- Reject or warn on duplicate names
- Optionally strip leading/trailing whitespace

### 4. "Cambia" (switch student) has no confirmation

Clicking "Cambia" in the nav immediately navigates to `/students/`, abandoning whatever the student was doing (mid-lesson, mid-drill). There's no "Are you sure?" confirmation.

**Fix:** Either add a simple confirmation dialog, or ensure lesson state is preserved so the student can resume.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] 404 and 403 errors render a styled HTML page with navigation
- [ ] Students can delete their own account from the student list or profile
- [ ] Student names are validated: max 30 chars, no duplicates (or at least a warning)
- [ ] Switching students mid-lesson either confirms or preserves lesson progress
